From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 02 Nov 2026 06:21:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/rockchip: dw_hdmi_qp: Always derive the link configuration in atomic_check

dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_check() skips the PHY setup and the
CRTC state update when the TMDS character rate, the color depth and the
bus format are those of the last call. Since the FRL support that
shortcut no longer covers the link configuration: an FRL link has the
same TMDS character rate as the TMDS link it replaces, so a modeset that
switches between TMDS and FRL at the same rate, depth and format is
taken as unchanged. The PHY stays in its old mode and the CRTC state
keeps the old frl_enabled, so the VOP still takes its DCLK from the
HDMI PHY PLL, and the FRL link training fails to set the TxFFE level,
which the PHY refuses in TMDS mode:

  FRL LTS:2 set_ffe_level failed: -22

Seen on an Orange Pi 5 when a sink's EDID (overridden to a 340 MHz
maximum TMDS character rate) makes 3840x2160@60Hz 8 bpc use FRL after
it ran over TMDS: the sink shows no signal, and every later modeset to
the same mode fails the same way.

The shortcut also keys on the rate of the last atomic check, which may
belong to a state that was refused or only tested and never committed,
while the CRTC state it leaves untouched is a copy of the committed one.

Drop it: the link configuration is cheap to derive, and phy_configure()
only records it for the next power-on anyway.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c | 7 -------
 1 file changed, 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
index ef3b927dac93..8e35d8ce25ff 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/rockchip/dw_hdmi_qp-rockchip.c
@@ -109,7 +109,6 @@ struct rockchip_hdmi_qp {
 	int hpd_irq;
 	int port_id;
 	const struct rockchip_hdmi_qp_ctrl_ops *ctrl_ops;
-	unsigned long long tmds_char_rate;
 	unsigned int phy_bpc;
 };
 
@@ -234,11 +233,6 @@ dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 	if (ingest_fmt < 0)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	if (hdmi->tmds_char_rate == conn_state->hdmi.tmds_char_rate &&
-	    s->output_bpc == conn_state->hdmi.output_bpc &&
-	    s->bus_format == ingest_fmt)
-		return 0;
-
 	switch (ingest_fmt) {
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB888_1X24:
 	case MEDIA_BUS_FMT_RGB101010_1X30:
@@ -293,7 +287,6 @@ dw_hdmi_qp_rockchip_encoder_atomic_check(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
 		return ret;
 	}
 
-	hdmi->tmds_char_rate = conn_state->hdmi.tmds_char_rate;
 	hdmi->phy_bpc = phy_cfg.hdmi.bpc;
 
 	s->output_type = DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA;
